---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '~/config/site.config';
const email = siteConfig.org.contactEmail;
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service" description="Terms of service for makepicsmall — a free, browser-based image compressor.">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: 2026-04-22</p>
  <div class="prose prose-slate mt-6 max-w-none">
    <p>
      Welcome to {siteConfig.identity.name}. By using this site you agree
      to the terms below. They are intentionally short. If you disagree
      with any part, please don't use the service.
    </p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      {siteConfig.identity.name} is a free, browser-based image compressor.
      All compression happens on your device. We do not charge for the
      tool and we do not require an account.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty — use at your own risk</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided <strong>"as is"</strong> and <strong>"as
      available"</strong>, without warranty of any kind, express or
      implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
      particular purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the
      service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or produce output
      suitable for any particular use. Always keep an original copy of
      important images; compression is a lossy process for JPG and WebP.
    </p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep all rights to any image you compress with the tool. Because
      images never leave your device, we never receive a copy and claim no
      rights. <strong>Do not use the tool to process images you do not own
      or have permission to use</strong>, or that contain illegal content.
      You are solely responsible for the content you process.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Don't try to break, reverse, or exploit the site beyond its normal UI.</li>
      <li>Don't use the site to violate any law or the rights of others.</li>
      <li>Don't attempt to overload, disrupt, or probe our infrastructure.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes to the service</h2>
    <p>
      We may change, suspend, or discontinue all or part of the service at
      any time without notice. We may also update these terms; the "last
      updated" date above reflects the most recent version.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, {siteConfig.identity.name},
      its operators, and its affiliates are not liable for any indirect,
      incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages — including
      lost data, lost profits, or corrupted files — arising from your use
      of or inability to use the service. Our aggregate liability for any
      claim relating to the service is limited to US $0, reflecting the
      fact that the service is provided free of charge.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which
      the site operator is established, without regard to conflict-of-law
      rules. Any dispute that cannot be resolved informally will be
      brought in the courts of that jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
